// mg_rhs — the fine-grid right-hand side b0, GENERIC over the stamp.
//
// Was: st_rhs inlined against the old 48-byte wave layout, which is why multigrid threw
// `requires (48) bytes ... supplied: (128)` against a richer stamp. Now it just calls
// st_rhs(c), so it inherits whatever sources/terms the stamp defines.
//
// DIMENSION-GENERIC (solver-ledger.md §7d): the cell math goes through ST_CELL / ST_OOB, and
// the b0 image declaration moved to the host so the image type can be 2D or 3D.
//
// The stamp declares h_curr (set 0), h_prev (set 1) and the push constant. Host must compile
// as: "#version 450" + local_size + `b0` @ set 3 + nd + stamp + this.

void main() {
    ST_IVEC c = ST_CELL();
    if (ST_OOB(c)) {
        return;
    }
    imageStore(b0, c, vec4(st_rhs(c), 0.0, 0.0, 0.0));
}
